xv6 — Priority Scheduler with Aging & Copy-on-Write Fork
=========================================================

This is a modified version of xv6-riscv for the Operating Systems
course at Universidad del Valle.  It implements:

  1. A priority-based scheduler with an aging mechanism.
  2. A Copy-on-Write (COW) fork() implementation.

Author:     Omar Esteban Agredo
Institution: Universidad del Valle
Course:      Operating Systems
Branch:      feature/scheduler-priority-aging

Build & run
-----------

    $ make clean
    $ make
    $ make qemu CPUS=1

Inside xv6:

    schedtest
    agingtest
    cowtest
    usertests -q

Upstream
--------

xv6 is a re-implementation of Unix Version 6 (v6) by Dennis Ritchie
and Ken Thompson, maintained at MIT for educational purposes.

    https://pdos.csail.mit.edu/6.1810/
